      {
        "type": "Module",
        "name": "power_amp_lm386",
        "description": "LM386 audio power amplifier acting as the final stage to drive an 8-ohm speaker. Powered by VIN_9V (VS pin) and GND. The preamplifier signal (AUDIO_MID) is AC-coupled into the non-inverting input (IN_POS), while IN_NEG is AC-grounded. The gain pins (GAIN_1 and GAIN_2) require a capacitor/resistor network to configure the LM386 gain, complementing the preamplifier to achieve the specified 100x-200x overall system gain. The BYPASS pin needs a decoupling capacitor. The output (VOUT) feeds the SPEAKER_OUT node via a large DC-blocking capacitor, and requires a standard Zobel network to ground to prevent high-frequency oscillation.",
        "id": "power_amp_lm386"
      },
